<sect2 id="docutils" xreflabel="docutils-&docutils-version;">

    <title>docutils-&docutils-version;</title>

    <indexterm zone="docutils">
      <primary sortas="a-docutils">docutils</primary>
    </indexterm>

    <sect3 role="package">
      <title>Introdução ao docutils</title>

      <para>
        &quot;<application>docutils</application>&quot; é um conjunto de módulos e
programas &quot;<application>Python</application>&quot; para processar
documentos de texto simples em formatos como &quot;HTML&quot;,
&quot;XML&quot; ou &quot;LaTeX&quot;.
      </para>

      &lfs130_checked;

      <bridgehead renderas="sect4">Informação do Pacote</bridgehead>
      <itemizedlist spacing="compact">
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Transferência (HTTP): <ulink url="&docutils-download-http;"/>
          </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Transferência (FTP): <ulink url="&docutils-download-ftp;"/>
          </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Soma de verificação MD5 da transferência: &docutils-md5sum;
          </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Tamanho da transferência: &docutils-size;
          </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Espaço em disco estimado exigido: &docutils-buildsize;
          </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Tempo de construção estimado: &docutils-time;
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </itemizedlist>

    </sect3>

    <sect3 role="installation">
      <title>Instalação do docutils</title>



      <!-- Editors note: Use - -root= instead of DESTDIR= when updating. -->
<para>
        Primeiro, remova alguns arquivos instalados em uma versão anterior que não
mais são válidos. Como o(a) usante &root;:
      </para>

<screen role="root"><userinput>for f in /usr/bin/rst*.py; do
  rm -fv /usr/bin/$(basename $f .py)
done</userinput></screen>

      <para>
        Para construir os aplicativos &quot;<application>Python
3</application>&quot;, execute o seguinte comando:
      </para>

&build-wheel;

      <para>
        Para instalar os aplicativos &quot;<application>Python</application>&quot;
execute o seguinte como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;&root;&quot;:
      </para>

<!-- FHS 3.0 section 4.4.2:
           "There must be no subdirectories in /usr/bin."
           But pip maintainers closed this as WONTFIX:
           https://github.com/pypa/pip/issues/6906

           No longer happening after the upstream removed .py suffix for
           /usr/bin scripts
      <para>

        To reduce the time needed for loading Python scripts,
        <command>pip3 install</command> will compile the scripts with
        extension <filename class='extension'>.py</filename> into byte code
        and save the result into
        <filename class='extension'>.pyc</filename> files in the directory
        <filename class='directory'>__pycache__</filename>.
        But this package installs <filename class='extension'>.py</filename>
        scripts into <filename class='directory'>/usr/bin</filename>.
        So the byte code files for them will be installed into
        <filename class='directory'>/usr/bin/__pycache__</filename>, which
        is not allowed by FHS.  Still as the &root; user, remove this
        directory:
      </para>

      <screen role="root"><userinput>rm -rfv /usr/bin/__pycache__</userinput></screen> -->
<!-- Don't try pytest.
           The test suite isn't compatible with pytest.  -->
<screen role="root"><userinput>&install-wheel; docutils</userinput></screen>

      

      
      <para>
        <!--Two tests in the
        <filename>
test_parser</filename> suite are known to fail.-->
Para testar a instalação, emita: <command>test/alltests.py</command>. 
      </para>
    </sect3>

